# Action tracker maintenance

- After each completed change set to software, packaging, documentation or the
  tracker, update the local root workbook `Action Items.xlsx` before reporting
  completion. Read-only discussions do not require a revision.
- Append one row to `Revision History` with the next RH identifier, date in
  America/New_York, change-set title, summary, validation, remaining manual
  checks and commit/reference. Use `Local working tree` until committed.
- Preserve previous revision entries and all existing workbook features.
  Update affected Actions rows only when implementation or actual test evidence
  justifies changing their status, follow-up or evidence.
- Distinguish automated/mock tests from physical hardware verification. Never
  mark a hardware test Verified solely because automated tests passed.
- Keep the workbook excluded from Git, installer bundles and GitHub releases.
  Do not force-add it or upload it. If it is absent on another checkout or
  locked, report the pending tracker update instead of silently skipping it.
